age on the closing date of the advertisement will be eligible Domicile Quota: Merit Job Location*: South Asian Studies, University of Cambridge, United Kingdom Test City(s): Islamabad Gender*: Male / Female Job Description/Duties: • The visiting fellow will engage with students and scholars on Pakistan’s history, culture, people, national and regional languages, eminent literary figures, geography and regional, economic and political environment in line with the academic requirements of the University. • The visiting fellow will engage with university staff in the teaching of Urdu, Pakistan Studies, Pakistani literature, history, society and culture at the University. • The visiting fellow will interact with academic community of the University with a view to positively contribute to the relations between Pakistani academic community and the University. • The visiting fellow will be encouraged to attend the weekly seminars held at the Centre of South Asian Studies during the academic year and other academic fora on relevant issues in the University. • The Visiting Fellow will engage with students and scholars of the University with a research interest in Pakistan as envisaged in the MOU. • The visiting fellow will be encouraged to work with University staff to organize and conduct conferences, seminars, symposia, workshops or Art exhibitions showcasing Pakistan’s culture; Read More Eligibility Criteria Qualifications PhD in Leadership & Management PhD in Usuluddin (Islamic Studies) PhD in Education PhD in English Literature PhD in English Linguistics PhD in Educational Leadership & Management PhD in Shariah (Islamic Law & Jurisprudence) PhD in Manufacturing Engineering & Management PhD in Sociology PhD in Special Education PhD in International Relations PhD in Management PhD in Business Administration PhD in Climate Change & Sustainable Development PhD in Islamic Banking & Finance PhD in Economics PhD in Architecture PhD in Media & Communication Studies PhD in Psych