 software is a big plus. Follow-ups with AGPR, MOITT for clearance funds and bills Will work under the direction of PM and PD. Maximum age: 45 Years. Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 8 Years Age Limit Max: 45 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.486045','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.305402','finance',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(115,'Project Officer (PPS08)','Pakistan Software Export Board (PSEB)','Pakistan','','4 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 19, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9651','njp','Project Officer (PPS-8) Qualification: Minimum 16 years of education from HEC recognized university in Management Sciences/Human Resource/Business Administration/Computer Sciences/IT Experience: Minimum 04 years of post-qualification experience in Human Resource Development / project management /capacity development projects. Preference will be given to those candidates with PSDP/ADP/Government Projects experience. Skills Required: Excellent communication skills, hands on experience in MS Project, MS Office. Skills to work under pressure and meet deadlines Flexibility and ability to work effectively as part of a team Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work effectively at all levels in a collaborative team environment Strong knowledge of ISO standards and Pakistan IT industry Well versed with office productivity, MS Project, MS Excel Internet and email applications Job Descriptions: Will report to Project Manager and will carry out project activities mainly planning, execution, coordination for timely initiation of the activities and completion of the tasks. Will perform routine Project related tasks and activities Facilitate in achieving set targets and implementation of short- and long-range goals. Monitor the progress of the activities and creation of progress reports. Drafting of ads, EOI\'s tenders and coordination with concerned for their publishing, assist in evaluation of bids/proposals and completion of file work. Perform such other tasks and duties assigned by the management from time to time. Perform milestone review with higher management Maximum Age: 45 Years Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 4 Years Age Limit Max: 45 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.488667','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.308733','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(116,'Assistant Manager Monitoring and Evaluation (PPS-8)','Pakistan Software Export Board (PSEB)','Pakistan','','4 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 19, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9652','njp','Qualification: Minimum 16 years of education from HEC recognized university in Management Sciences/Human Resource/Business Administration/Computer Sciences/IT/Project Management Experience: Minimum 04 years of post-qualification in project management/ monitoring and evaluation of projects with at least 3 years of working in PSDP Projects Skills Required: Excellent knowledge of project management (Planning, Organizing, Budgeting, Execution etc.) Excellent communication/ presentation skills with fluency in written and spoken English Flexibility and ability to work effectively as part of a team Well versed with office productivity, MS Project, Excel, & Other international project management tools Job Descriptions: Will report to Project Manager and will be responsible for planning and successful execution of the project activities strictly in line with PC-1 and scope of the Project. Contract management including drafting of contracts, execution of the contracts and dispute resolution. Responsible for submission and approval of cash plans and release of funds, monitoring of the project team. Ensure procurements as per PPRA and applicable rules and regulations. Also ensure that record of the Project has been maintained properly and information related to the project is available as and when required by the Director Projects, management, MoITT, Planning, Audits and the Project Committees. Ensure resource availability and allocation as per direction of Supervisor Assist in performing routine project related tasks and activities and perform duties as assigned by Project Director Regular follow-ups on release of funds with Ministry of IT and other Govt. Departments Responsible for convening of project committees’ meetings and seeking of required approvals before initiation of any project related activity. Issue office letters, office orders, meeting minutes, Issue office letters, office orders, preparation of meeting minutes Perform milestone review visits along with higher management Maximum Age: 45 Years Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 4 Years Age Limit Max: 45 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.491335','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.311766','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(117,'Digital Expert FDI','Ministry of Information Technology and Telecommunication (MOITT)','Pakistan','','8 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 20, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9653','njp','INTRODUCTION: Pioneering Digital Growth: Leading Pakistan’s Charge in Global Digital Investment. Pakistan, with its dynamic population of over 240 million and a surging digital landscape, stands at a pivotal moment. The Ministry of Information Technology and Telecommunication seeks a visionary Digital Expert FDI (SPPS-II) to position Pakistan as a premier global destination for digital foreign direct investment. This is not just another senior role; it’s a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to directly influence the technological and economic trajectory of a rapidly evolving economy. This position offers you unparalleled strategic exposure, leadership experience, and the satisfaction of building a legacy that impacts generations to come. QUALIFICATIONS & EXPERIENCE: We welcome candidates with diverse backgrounds, investment and economic development professionals, public policy and regulatory experts, or telecom sector specialists with public or private sector experience. The ideal candidate combines a passion for public good with the ability to navigate Pakistan\'s complex investment, regulatory, and digital economy landscape. Education: Masters Degree from reputable HEC / internationally recognized university in the related field of Electrical / Computer Sciences / Electronics / Telecommunication / Information Technology / Business Management. Professional Expertise: 1. At least 8 years of relevant experience in IT & Telecom sector including exposure to international engagements and government / regulatory affairs. 2. Demonstrated experience working on digital economy or emerging technology issues (e.g., fiberization, spectrum, IoT, OTT services, smart cities, digital infrastructure), reflecting the ability to work across sector growth, policy, and technology domains. Core Competencies: 1. Strong cross-sectoral coordination and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with ministries, regulatory bodies, international institutions, and the Minister\'s Office, translating complex technical/policy matters into clear, actionable briefs and recommendations. 2. Ability to manage multiple concurrent workstreams, investment pitchbooks and policy inputs to parliamentary briefs, ministerial correspondence, and event/initiative support with strong organizational and prioritization skills under tight government timelines. Key Responsibilities: 1. Project Proposals and Investment Pitchbooks: Develop export-led investment proposals, project documents, and investment pitchbooks for the Telecom sector; vet investment proposals; identify investment potential focused on national needs, sustainability, and global/regional best practices, and develop supporting guidelines and SOPs. 2. Taxation and Budget Proposals: Contribute to the formulation and review of taxation and budget proposals affecting the digital economy and Telecom sector, in coordination with relevant stakeholders ensuring alignment with fiscal policy objectives. 3. Interministerial Coordination: Coordinate with other ministries and government departments to align policy positions, resolve cross-cutting issues, and ensure coherent whole-of-government action. 4. International Engagements: Represent and support MoITT\'s engagement with international and regional platforms and institutions, including but not limited to CPEC, ECO, DCO, CAREC, the World Bank, ADB, SCO, and CTO, etc. on matters relating to digital economy investment and cooperation. 5. Bilateral MoUs: Assist in the negotiation, drafting, and processing of bilateral Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) and agreements with foreign governments/organizations relating to digital economy and IT/Telecom cooperation. 6. Parliamentary Coordination: Manage and support coordination with the Senate and National Assembly, including preparation of responses to parliamentary questions, briefs for committee proceedings and legislative business where required. 7. Ministry Reports: Contribute to the preparation of the Ministry\'s annual and quarterly reports, documenting achievements and progress. 8. Initiatives/Events: Support the planning and execution of national initiatives and events (e.g., Ramzan Package, BISP, Flood Response), ensuring the Ministry\'s effective participation and representation. 9. Minister\'s Office Coordination: Coordinate with the Minister\'s Office, prepare talking points and briefing notes. 10. Ministry Initiatives/Projects: Coordinate and track flagship Ministry initiatives and projects. 11. PSDP Projects Review: Assist in the monitoring and review of PSDP-funded projects under the Ministry, tracking and implementation progress. 12. Emerging Technologies Policy & Coordination: Formulate and coordinate policy on emerging technology areas including OTT services, IoT, smartphones (accessibility, financing, and device standards), fintech/digital financial services, and smart city initiatives, ensuring the regulatory framework keeps pace with evolving digital trends. 13. Other Duties: Perform any other task assigned from time to time. 1. Policy & Regulatory Coordination: Produce timely, quality inputs on taxation, budget, and regulatory proposals (in coordination with FBR, BoI, SIFC, PTA) resulting in at least one documented policy/regulatory improvement per year that reduces investment barriers. 2. International & Bilateral Engagement: Represent MoITT effectively at international platforms (CPEC, ECO, DCO, CAREC, WB, ADB, SCO, CTO) and progress bilateral MoUs/agreements for sector growth and investments. 3. Reporting & Parliamentary/Ministerial Support: Ensure on-time submission of quarterly/annual reports, parliamentary responses, and ministerial briefing notes. DURATION: Appointment of the Digital Expert FDI, SPPS-II Scale shall initially be made on contract basis initially for a period of two (2) years extendable for another term of two-year contingent upon result-based performance as per general criteria applicable for appointment against the positions of Special Professional Pay Scales (SPPS) already issued, or to be issued, from the Establishment Division of the Federal Government from time to time. MANNER OF APPOINTMENT: The appointment shall be made as per prescribed procedure of appointment in SPPS positions. a) The vacancy shall be advertised at least in two national leading newspapers and uploaded on its website of the Ministry and National Job Portal and also advertised. b) An in-house committee shall be constituted under the chair of the Additional Secretary, MoITT for scrutiny of the applications for placement before the Special Selection Board. c) The Special Selection Board for selection against the Special Professional Pay Scales shall recommend candidate(s) for appointment with the approval of the competent authority as per SPPS Policy of the Federal Government. PAY PACKAGE: The Digital Expert FDI, SPPS-II Scale, shall receive pay package of SPPS-II Scale in accordance with the SPPS Policy, 2024 of the Federal Government as amended from time to time. LEAVE: The incumbent shall earn leave on full pay @ 3 days per month for the period of duty. The leave shall be availed during the currency of contract period as per policy of the Federal Government. TERMINATION OF CONTRACT: The contract of Digital Expert FDI, SPPS-II shall be terminated according to the SPPS Policy of the Federal Government on one month\'s notice on either side or payment of one month\'s basic pay in lieu thereof. In respect of matters not specified here, the law, rules, policies corresponding level of Civil Servants shall be applicable as per SPPS Policy of the Federal Government. Read More Eligibility Criteria Qualifications BS Computer Science (BSCS) BS Information Technology (BSIT) BS Telecommunication & Networking BS Opto-Electronics & Laser Engineering BS Electrical Engineering (power) BBA (Information Technology) MBA (Information Technology) MSc Computer Science MS Computer Science (MSCS) MS Information Technology (MSIT) PhD in Electrical Engineering PhD in Information Technology PhD in Electrical Engineering (Power) PhD in Computer Science PhD in Telecommunication Engineering Master of Computer Science (MCS) BE Computer Science BS Telecommunication Engineering BS Electronics Engineering BE Information Technology BS Electronics MSc Information Technology MS Telecommunication & Networking BS Electrical Engineering (General) BE Electronics Engineering BE Telecommunications BE Electrical (Telecom) MS Telecommunication Engineering MS Electronics Engineering BE Electrical Engineering MSc (Hons) Telecommunication Networks BE Telecommunication Engineering MSc Telecommunication Systems BS Electronics and Communication MSc Electronics MS Electrical Engineering BS Electrical Engineering (Telecommunication) MPhil Computer Science MPhil Electronics PhD in Electronics BE Electrical (Electronics) BS Electrical Technology PhD in Electronics Engineering BA (Hons) Business Management BSc Electrical Engineering Technology BS Electrical Engineering PhD in Microelectronics & Applied Physics MBA (Information Technology Management) BSc Electrical Engineering (Electronics) MSc Engineering Business Management MSc Electrical Engineering MSc Telecommunication Engineering BS.Tech Electrical BS.Tech Electronics BS.Tech Telecommunications BS Electronics Engineering Technology BS Electrical Engineering (Electronics) B.Tech (Hons) Electronics B.Tech (Hons) Electrical MPhil Information Technology BSc Electrical Engineering (Telecommunications) Master of Engineering (Information Technology) BS Business Management & Accounting BSc Electrical and Computer Engineering MSc Operational Telecommunications MS(Electronic Design) PhD in Electronic Engineering (Telecom) BS Telecommunication BS Electrical (Computer) Engineering MSc Strategic Business Management MSc Information Technology Management BSc Electrical Engineering (Power) MS business Management BSc Electronics Engineering Master of Information Technology- MIT BSc Telecommunication Engineering MPhil Microelectronics Engineering & Semiconductor Physics MSc in Electronic Commerce BSc (Hons.) Business Management & Marketing BS Agriculture and Agribusiness management MSc Digital Business Managment Bachelors of Business and Information Technology (BBIT) Master of Computer Science (Executive) EMCS Masters in Agribusiness Management M.E Electrical Power Engineering Masters of Telecommunications M.E Telecommunication BE Industrial Electronics Engineering (IIEE) MS Computer and Information Technology Bachelors of Computer Science MBA (Business Management) Msc in Artificial Intelligence and Computer Science Master of Business and Information Technology (Finance) MS Telecommunication & Networks BS Telecommunication Systems PhD in Telecommunication & Networks MPhil Electrical Engineering MPhil Electronics Engineering MPhil Telecommunication Engineering MPhil Telecommunication and Networks MSc in Control and Electronics MS Computer Science and Information Technology Read More Experience 8 Years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.494024','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.314874','other',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(118,'Head of AI','Ignite - National Technology Fund','Pakistan','','12 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 25, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9654','njp','Head of AI shall lead the implementation, coordination, and operational management of the National AI Innovation Hub (NAIIH) and other AI-related initiatives undertaken by Ignite. Reporting to the GM Projects, the position shall be responsible for overseeing programme execution, stakeholder coordination, project governance, and the achievement of approved objectives related to AI ecosystem development. The role shall support the planning, implementation, monitoring, and continuous improvement of national AI programmes while working closely with government stakeholders, industry partners, academia, development partners, and technology ecosystem participants. The incumbent shall provide technical and strategic guidance on AI-related initiatives and contribute towards strengthening Pakistan\'s AI innovation and infrastructure landscape in line with Ignite\'s mandate and strategic priorities. As the lead position for AI programmes within the Projects Dept. Head of AI shall oversee programme delivery, vendor and operator performance, and the alignment of implementation activities with approved objectives and national priorities. The position shall coordinate with the Ministry of Information Technology & Telecommunication (MoITT), relevant government entities, industry stakeholders, academia, and ecosystem partners to ensure effective programme execution and ecosystem development. Head of AI shall support institutional decision-making by providing subject matter expertise on AI technologies, governance frameworks, and emerging trends. The role shall also contribute to the development of future AI initiatives, policy recommendations, ecosystem growth strategies, and programme expansion opportunities, while ensuring effective governance, compliance, performance management, and long-term sustainability of AI-related programmes. Key Responsibilities • Lead the implementation, coordination, and operational management of the National AI Innovation Hub (NAIIH) and related AI initiatives undertaken by Ignite. • Provide strategic and technical leadership for the planning, execution, monitoring, and continuous improvement of AI infrastructure and ecosystem development programmes. • Support the development and implementation of Pakistan\'s sovereign AI ecosystem by ensuring alignment of programme activities with approved objectives, national priorities, and Ignite\'s strategic mandate. • Oversee programme delivery and monitor the performance of operators, vendors, consultants, and implementation partners to ensure compliance with contractual obligations, service levels, and performance targets. • Provide technical oversight of AI compute infrastructure, AI platforms, data repositories, and related services delivered under the NAIIH programme. • Review and provide recommendations on technical architectures, solution designs, infrastructure enhancements, and major change requests related to AI programmes. • Support the development of foundation models, Urdu and regional language AI capabilities, AI-as-a-Service offerings, and other initiatives aimed at strengthening Pakistan\'s AI ecosystem. • Contribute to the development and implementation of governance frameworks, security controls, data management standards, and compliance requirements applicable to AI programmes. • Coordinate with the Ministry of Information Technology & Telecommunication (MoITT), government entities, development partners, academia, industry stakeholders, and ecosystem participants to facilitate programme implementation and stakeholder engagement. • Provide technical and strategic inputs to senior management on AI infrastructure, ecosystem development, emerging technologies, programme risks, and future expansion opportunities. • Support procurement activities, contract management processes, and evaluation of proposals relating to AI infrastructure, platforms, services, and ecosystem initiatives. • Prepare and present programme progress reports, technical briefings, risk assessments, and recommendations for management, committees, and other relevant stakeholders. • Establish and maintain effective programme governance, performance monitoring mechanisms, and institutional coordination frameworks for AI-related initiatives. • Lead, mentor, and develop the AI programme team to strengthen technical capability, knowledge management, and programme delivery effectiveness. • Perform any other assignments related to AI programmes and ecosystem development as may be assigned by the GM Projects from time to time. Qualification & Experience • Master’s degree in Computing, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a closely related discipline from a recognised institution. • Minimum 12 years of progressive experience in the design, procurement, or implementation of large-scale digital systems. • Demonstrated leadership of national-scale digital platforms or programmes, with accountability for delivery outcomes and stakeholder engagement. • Experience advising on programme design and procurement specifications for national digital infrastructure, ideally including AI, HPC, or data platform initiatives. • Experience of managed-services or vendor-delivered programmes, including governance of third-party operators against SLAs. Knowledge & Skills • Working understanding of sovereign AI infrastructure, cloud and hybrid compute, data platforms, and integration architectures. • Familiarity with AI governance, responsible-AI principles, and applicable national data protection frameworks. • Procurement and contract governance — RFP/TOR drafting, bid evaluation, performance-based contracting, and SLA frameworks. • Cybersecurity fundamentals — IAM, zero-trust principles, and security specifications for sovereign AI infrastructure. • Senior stakeholder engagement and ministry-level advisory presence. • Sound judgement on trade-offs between innovation enablement, security posture, and fiscal sustainability. Read More Eligibility Criteria Qualifications Master of Engineering Master of Technology (MTech) MSc Computer Science MSc Intelligent Systems & Robotics MS Robotics & AI Engineering MS Innovation & Entrepreneurship MS Computer Science (MSCS) MS Information Technology (MSIT) Master of Computer Science (MCS) MS Data Science MSc Information Technology MSc Network Systems MS Computer Software Engineering MSc (Hons) Telecommunication Networks MSc Telecommunication Systems Master in Sustainable International Development MS Information Security MS Cybersecurity MS Computer Networks MS Computer Systems Engineering MS Computational Sciences & Engineering ME Computer Systems Engineering MS Computer Engineering MS Artificial Intelligence MS Innovative Technologies in Learning Master of Engineering (Information Technology) MSc Operational Telecommunications MS Data Analytics MSc Information Technology Management MSc. Computer Engineering Msc Cybersecurity and Data governance MSc Computational Mathematics Master of Engineering (Software Engineering) MS Robotics and Intelligent Machine Engineering MS Intelligence and Security Studies Masters of science in Information Systems Master of Computer Science (Executive) EMCS Masters of Telecommunications MS Computer and Network Security MS Computer and Information Technology MSc Information and Communication Technology MSC Data Communication & Networks Msc International Business with Data Analytics Msc in Artificial Intelligence and Computer Science MS Cyber Forensics MS Network Security MS Information Systems MSc Innovative Technology MS Computer Science and Information Technology Master in Science Technology and Innovation Management and Policy Read More Experience 12 Years Age Limit Max: 55 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.497168','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.319087','other',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(119,'Senior Officer – Treasury Settlements','EXIM Bank of Pakistan','Pakistan','','3 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 22, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9655','njp','Qualification: Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Business Administration, or related field from a leading local or international university recognised by the Higher Education Commission of Pakistan(H.E.C.). Experience: Minimum of 3(three) years of professional relevant experience in a Treasury of a bank(s), DFI(s), NBFI(s) or brokerage house(s). Key Responsibilities: Effectively check, verify transactions in accordance with Treasury/Investment Policy, ensuring processing of transactions is carried out in a timely manner and ensuring proper settlement of transactions.  Effectively check the compliance of Treasury Operation Processes and improve the control process to identify/mitigate risks.  Prepare daily, weekly and monthly reports of Treasury Back-Office.  Coordinate with back-offices of the counterparties and brokers for the settlement of the transactions.  Manage the bank’s securities executed in the back-office operations covering the whole value chain from trade clearing, settlement to custody operation, liaising with Finance Operations of the bank as part of the value chain.  Coordinate with Manager Treasury for Training and Development of the Treasury Back-Office team.  Any other task assigned by the Line Management. Core Competence: Good knowledge of Treasury benchmarks, settlement of back-office transactions, reporting frameworks, regulatory and statutory requirements.  Well versed with SBP’s RTGS system.  Good computer literacy and inclination towards automation.  Ability to work independently and create goals and vision for delivery in ambiguous, difficult or new situations.  Excellent team player.  Able to take up challenges. Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 3 Years Age Limit Max: 55 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.500131','Regular','2026-09-11 23:27:22.322567','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(120,'CEO, PHA Foundation','PHA Foundation','Pakistan','','15 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 24, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9661','njp','PHA Foundation (PHAF) is a State-Owned Enterprise of the Government of Pakistan, established under Section 42 of the Companies Act, 2017 with the mandate to promote, facilitate and regulate affordable housing schemes and urban development projects across Pakistan. PHAF invites applications from suitably qualified, proactive and dynamic professionals for the position of Full time Chief Executive Officer (CEO), in accordance with State-Owned Enterprises (Governance and Operations) Act, 2023, State Owned Enterprise (C-Level Appointments) Guidelines 2024 issued by the Central Monitoring Unit (CMU), Finance Division and the Public Sector Companies (CEO Appointment) Guidelines, 2015. The candidate should possess: i. Demonstrated experience of providing vision, leading and managing multiple teams of top professionals and delivering concrete and measurable results in a demanding corporate environment; and ii. Demonstrated experience of evaluating and applying emerging technologies to transform businesses and deliver sustainable competitive advantage; and iii. Strong and proven past experience of large scale project management and supervision; and iv. Good interpersonal and communication skills (written, verbal and listening) along with being a team builder. Joining Eligibility Criteria i. At least Master’s degree or equivalent (16 years of education) in Urban Planning, Architecture, Development studies, Business Administration, Public Administration, Finance, Engineering, or equivalent from a HEC Recognised University/ Degree Awarding Institute. Foreign credentials will be given additional weightage. ii. A minimum of fifteen (15) years of relevant professional experience, including substantial experience at senior management positions, with demonstrated expertise in project management, construction sector, infrastructure development or equivalent field. iii. Candidates having successfully served Public Sector Entities / Corporations as CEO/MD will be given preference. iv. Strong knowledge of government laws, rules and policies related to project management, public procurement and public financial management is mandatory. v. The candidate must not have attained the age of 50 years as at the closing date of application. Pay/ Remuneration A market-competitive remuneration package shall be offered to the selected Chief Executive Officer of PHAF, as determined by the Board of Directors. Terms and Conditions i. The position of CEO PHAF is based at Islamabad. ii. Applicants shall submit a detailed CV, valid CNIC, attested and HEC/relevant body verified academic credentials, HEC Equivalence Certificate (for foreign qualifications), professional registration (where applicable), recent photographs, NOC (for government employees) and experience certificates specifying designation, duration and nature of employment. iii. True copies of all submission will be required from the short-listed Candidates at the time of interview. iv. Civil servants meeting the aforesaid criteria may also apply, subject to pre-requisite NOCs from parent Ministry/Department and/or Cadre Administrative. v. The initial contract shall be for a period of three (03) years, with an annual performance evaluation to be conducted by the Board of Directors against Board-approved Key Performance Indicators (KPIs). The contract may be extended for a further period of up to two (02) years on the basis of satisfactory performance, subject to the Board\'s resolution and concurrence of the competent authority under the SOE Act, 2023. vi. The candidate must meet the Fit and Proper Criteria as laid down in Schedule IV of the State-Owned Enterprises (Governance and Operations) Act, 2023 and the SOE (C-Level Appointments) Guidelines 2024. Any person disqualified under these instruments shall not be eligible. vii. A declaration on stamp paper of Rs. 100/- or above duly verified by the Oath Commissioner, confirming eligibility to hold the position in accordance with the Schedule II of CMU Guidelines for C- level appointments, shall be mandatory at the time of application (to be attached with CV on National Job Portal). viii. The recommendations/ selection/ tenure of the candidate shall be subject to applicable Government law, rules, regulations, policy, instructions issued from time to time. ix. PHAF is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate, subject to the fitness for the job, specific experience and Government of Pakistan’s regulations; x. PHAF reserves the right to cancel withdraw or amend the advertisement or selection process at any stage. xi. Only eligible/ shortlisted candidates will be called for interview. No TA/DA will be admissible for interview purpose; xii. Eligible candidates are required to submit their applications, along with all the aforementioned supporting documents, within fifteen (15) days from the date of publication of this advertisement. Mandatory: DECLARATION TO ACCOMPANY THE APPLICATION FORM FOR THE POST OF CHIEF EXECUTIVE OF PUBLIC SECTOR COMPANY i. I…………………..Son/Daughter of ………………., holder of CNIC No………………… hereby declare that I am not ineligible to act as a………………….in terms of Fit and Proper Criteria under the SOEs Act. ii. I further declare that I am not suffering from any present or perceived conflict of interests which would interfere with the exercise of independent judgment when acting in the capacity of ……………… of the Company or would be disadvantageous to the interests of the SOEs. Signature: Full Name (In Block Letters)………………………………… Designation, NIC Number, and Full Address Date………………….. Place…………………. Witness to the signature: Signature: Full Name…………………………………………….. Father’s, Husband’s name:……………………………… Name (In Block letters), NIC Number, Occupation, Full Address. Note: To be made on stamp paper of requisite amount duly verified by Oath Commissioner Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 15 Years Age Limit Max: 50 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.520534','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.326216','other',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(121,'Manager Property and Land','Pakistan Railways Headquarter Office','Pakistan','','5 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 26, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9663','njp','Bachelor’s Degree in Civil Engineering or equivalent qualification registration with PEC having 05 years relevant experience of land management or equivalent Vacancy 1 (Merit) Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 5 Years Age Limit Max: 62 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.523491','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.329534','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(122,'Manager Legal','Pakistan Railways Headquarter Office','Pakistan','','5 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 26, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9664','njp','Bachelor Degree in Law (LLB) or MBA or any other relevant degree having 05 years post-qualification in the relevant field. Vacancy 1 (Merit) Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 5 Years Age Limit Max: 62 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.526189','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.332539','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(123,'Manager Contract','Pakistan Railways Headquarter Office','Pakistan','','5 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 26, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9665','njp','Master in Business Administration (Marketing/Finance) or Master of Law (LLM) having 05 years post qualification experience in the relevant field. (Contract Management) Vacancy 1 (Merit) Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 5 Years Age Limit Max: 62 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.528855','Contract','2026-09-11 23:27:22.336199','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(124,'Manager Geographical Information System (GIS)','Pakistan Railways Headquarter Office','Pakistan','','5 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 26, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9666','njp','Master degree in Geographical Inform