irectors. ii. Report company performance to the Board. iii. Provide inspired leadership; create culture of performance, positive morale and accountability in the company. iv. Provide a marketing plan and the vision of the company\'s future development. v. Lead development and execution of short and long-term operational policies and strategic plans for the company. vi. Assess risks to the company and ensure they are monitored and minimized. vii. Bear responsibilities for the company\'s finances, including working closely with the CFO to prepare budgets. and keep the Board of Directors informed with respect to cash management, investments and internal audits. viii. Work closely with Human Resources (HR) to streamline hiring practices, fixation of perks, privileges and benefit disbursement of the employees. ix. Oversee quality control throughout the company, establishing goals for each department in partnership with division managers. x. Assure all legal and regulatory documents are filed and monitor compliance with laws and regulations. xi. Represent the company as required, including attendance at important functions, industry events and public meetings and create alliance for the company, if required. xii. Evaluate the work of other executives within the company. xiii. Ensure that the company maintains high social impact and adhere to its corporate social responsibility. All other responsibilities mentioned in all applicable laws. Eligibility will be determined and selection will be finalized as per approved government policy. The selection and compensation will be determined by the BoD. Only shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. The candidate shall not be entitled for any TA/DA while appearing for the interview. No person shall be appointed as Chief Executive Officer unless he is a citizen of Pakistan. Dual Nationality holders will not be considered. Interested candidates must send CV, copies of certificates and degrees, CNIC and two recent passport size photographs. \"The remuneration package will be determined based on the candidate\'s experience and competence\". The position is based at Head Office Karachi. Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 10 Years Age Limit Max: 62 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.581272','Contract','2026-09-13 20:38:19.581281','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(238,'Assistant Director (IT Networks & Infrastructure)','Frequency Allocation Board','Pakistan','','5 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 27, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9686','njp','Qualification: Four-year Bachelor’s degree in Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, IT, or relevant field (HEC recognized, Min CGPA 3.5 or 75% marks). Experience & Skills: Minimum 05 years of post-qualification experience in network administration and troubleshooting (TCP/IP, VLANs, subnetting, routing, switching, STP, DHCP, DNS, NAT). Configuration and administration of Layer-2/Layer-3 switches, routers, enterprise firewalls, IPsec/SSL VPNs, network security controls, virtualization platforms (VMware, Hyper-V, Proxmox), server backup/recovery, and network monitoring tools (PRTG, Zabbix, Wireshark). Master\'s degree, PEC/NCEAC registration, and certifications (CCNA, CCNP, CompTIA Network+) preferred. Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 5 Years Age Limit Max: 32 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.584997','Regular','2026-09-13 20:38:19.585004','technology',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(239,'Assistant Director (Software)','Frequency Allocation Board','Pakistan','','5 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 27, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9687','njp','Four-year Bachelor’s degree in Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, IT or any other relevant field from a reputed local or foreign university, duly recognized & verified by HEC, with a Minimum CGPA of 3.5 or 75% marks. Minimum 05 years of post-qualification experience in relevant field from a reputed public/private sector ICT organization. Preferred Skills: Network administration and troubleshooting (TCP/IP, VLANs, subnetting, routing, switching, STP, DHCP, DNS, NAT), Layer-2/Layer-3 switches, enterprise firewalls, IPsec/SSL VPNs, network monitoring tools (PRTG, Zabbix, Nagios, ntopng, Wireshark), network segmentation, virtualization platforms (VMware, Hyper-V, Proxmox), and server backup/recovery. Certifications (CCNA, CCNP, CompTIA Network+), Master\'s degree (18 years), and valid registration from PEC or NCEAC preferred. Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 5 Years Age Limit Max: 32 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.588036','Regular','2026-09-13 20:38:19.588044','technology',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(240,'Assistant Director (Cyber Security)','Frequency Allocation Board','Pakistan','','5 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 27, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9688','njp','Four years Bachelor\'s degree in Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, IT, Cyber Security or any other relevant field from a reputed local or foreign university, duly recognized & verified by HEC, with a Minimum CGPA of 3.5 or 75% marks. Minimum 05 years of post-qualification experience, with at least 2 years in Governance, Risk Management and Compliance (GRC) roles in private/government/telecom/banking sector. Preferred Skills: Security frameworks & regulatory requirements (PISF 2026, CERT Rules 2023, ISO/IEC 27001, NIST, CIS Controls), Information Security Policies & SOPs, Information Security Risk Assessment, Risk Registers, Cybersecurity Incident Response, VAPT (Applications, Web, Network, Systems), SIEM platforms, security monitoring, and firewall controls. Master\'s degree (18 years) and valid registration from PEC or NCEAC preferred. Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 5 Years Age Limit Max: 32 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.591060','Regular','2026-09-13 20:38:19.591068','administration',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(241,'Manager Data and Research','Pakistan Software Export Board (PSEB)','Pakistan','','4 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 27, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9689','njp','Position: Manager Data & Research Reports to: Director Industry Facilitation Department: Business Development & Industry Facilitation Location: Islamabad Maximum Age: 50 years Role Overview: Serve as PSEB\'s central resource for organizational data, analytics, industry intelligence, research and management reporting. The position will work under the supervision of Director Industry Facilitation, providing analytical support across PSEB functions for data-driven planning, decision-making, performance monitoring and policy inputs. The role involves access to sensitive institutional, company-level and inter-agency data; the incumbent is required to maintain strict confidentiality of all such data and information accessed in the course of duty, in accordance with PSEB\'s data governance and confidentiality policies. Educational Qualification: • Minimum 16 years of education (Master\'s degree or equivalent) in Data Science / Statistics / Computer Science / Information Technology / Economics / Engineering / Business Analytics or a related discipline. • Candidates from other disciplines with relevant experience in data analysis / research or business intelligence are also encouraged to apply. • Degree(s) must be from a HEC-recognized national or international university/institution. Experience: • Minimum 4 years of post-qualification experience in data analysis / business intelligence / research / performance monitoring / industry analytics or a related field. • Hands-on experience with business intelligence and data visualization tools such as Power BI / Tableau / Looker Studio or equivalent. • Working knowledge of SQL and/or advanced spreadsheet-based analysis. • Experience in data collection frameworks / survey tools / dataset management / performance indicators / management reporting systems. • Working knowledge of data cleaning / validation / quality assurance practices across data sources. • Ability to convert data into dashboards / reports / presentations for management and decision-makers. • Strong written and verbal communication skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple assignments and deadlines. Preferred / Added Advantage: • Experience in the public sector / ICT industry / consulting / development sector. • Working knowledge of Python / R for data transformation / automation / statistical analysis / forecasting. • Understanding of Pakistan\'s IT and ITeS sector / ICT exports / technology companies / skills landscape / public-sector data structures. • Relevant certifications in data analytics / business intelligence / visualization / statistical analysis or related areas. Key Responsibilities: • Data Management and Governance: Act as the central focal person for PSEB-wide data, maintaining structured, reliable and up-to-date datasets across exports, companies, industry facilitation, skills, projects, events, delegations and infrastructure. • ICT Export Analysis and Forecasting: Maintain and analyze Pakistan\'s ICT export data by market, region, service category and trend. Prepare periodic export analyses, forecasts and performance comparisons for management. • Industry Intelligence and Roundups: Prepare periodic industry roundups and sector snapshots covering export performance, company activity, technology trends, talent indicators, policy changes and competitor-country developments. • Company Data Collection and Analysis: Develop and maintain company-level datasets, profiles, export markets, service lines, capabilities, workforce, certifications, partnerships to support market access and industry facilitation. • Lead, Event and Program Analytics: Track leads, qualified opportunities, MoUs, contracts and outcomes from PSEB-supported events, delegations and programs, and prepare performance and ROI analysis. • Dashboards and Executive Reporting: Develop and maintain management dashboards, visual reports and scorecards for approved PSEB stakeholders, covering exports, companies, programs, leads and institutional KPIs. • Research and International Benchmarking: Conduct primary and secondary research on emerging technologies and market opportunities, and benchmark Pakistan\'s positioning against regional and international competitors. • Impact and Policy Analysis: Assess the impact of tax incentives / policy measures / industry facilitation initiatives, and provide analytical inputs for policy development and strategic reviews. • Stakeholder Coordination: Coordinate with internal PSEB departments and relevant external public/private entities to obtain, reconcile, validate and integrate datasets through approved institutional arrangements, as guided by the Director Industry Facilitation. • Project and Institutional Support: Provide analytical support for PC-1s, project proposals, third-party evaluations, annual reports and national benchmarking exercises. • Data Quality, Standardization and Automation: Establish common data definitions, reporting templates and quality standards, and identify opportunities to automate recurring data collection and reporting processes. • Undertake priority analytical assignments, research requests and data briefs as directed by the Director Industry Facilitation • Any other duties assigned by the line management. Read More Eligibility Criteria Experience 4 Years Age Limit Max: 50 years','2026-09-13 20:38:19.594109','Contract','2026-09-13 20:38:19.594117','research',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(242,'Consultant – Economics (SPPS-III)','Ministry of Planning, Development & Special Initiatives','Pakistan','','7 Years+','','[]','Available Till Sep 28, 2026','https://www.njp.gov.pk/jobs/9705','njp','JOB DESCRIPTION OF CONSULTANT, ECONOMICS i. To develop and apply economic models to assess the impact of various policies and strategies. ii. To conduct cost-benefit analyses to inform decision-making processes. iii. To provide expert advice on economic aspects of sectoral (i.e. energy) planning and policy formulation. iv. To assist in the development of strategies to promote sustainable economic growth through effective management of available resource base. v. To oversee the collection, analysis, and interpretation of economic data related to economic interventions in terms of policies and projects. vi. To prepare comprehensive analytical reports and present to the stakeholders. vii. To collaborate with government agencies, private sector entities, and international organizations to align economic strategies with national development goals. viii. To provide training and mentorship to junior economists and staff within the Planning Commission. ix. To promote a culture of continuous learning and improvement in economic analysis and knowledge sharing practices. x. To interpret complex socio-economic data and provide actionable insights periodically. xi. To interpret complex data and provide actionable insights from time to time. xii. To carry out any other task assigned by Secretary, Member, DCPC and Minister PD&SI. Read More Eligibility Criteria Qualifications BS Social Work BS Accounting & Finance BS Banking & Finance BS Business Administration BS Commerce BS Management BS Marketing BS Public Administration BS Arabic BS Translation & Interpretation BS Computer Science (BSCS) BS Aviation Management BS Aviation Professional Pilot (APP) BS Aerospace Engineering BS Avionics Engineering BS Maritime Sciences BS GIS & Remote Sensing BS Nanoscience & Technology BE Mining Engineering BS Petroleum & Gas Engineering BS Artificial Intelligence BS Software Engineering BS Data Science BS Cybersecurity BS Bioinformatics BS Information Systems BS Multimedia & Gaming BS Information Technology (BSIT) BS Computer Engineering BS Hardware Engineering BS Mechanical Engineering BS Civil Engineering BS Economics BS Economics & Finance BS Islamic Banking & Finance BS English BS Persian BS Urdu BS Financial Technology & E-Commerce BS Business Analytics BS Biotechnolo